(966858, 111309, 9763, '<td valign="top">I saw your thread on "freaking hypocrits" post and i wanted to offer you my critique to maybe help you out a little.  <br/> <br/>Composition: it works well, but could be cropped a tiny bit tighter on the top and a little looser on the bottom<br/>Color: way too blue.  I would say you should warm this up a bit for a more natural look<br/>Focus: the fingers are clear in some locations (i see one pretty clear finger nail) and a few buttons on the remote are clear, but not enough clarity in the image.  The DOF is fine for the face and body, but the hand and remote should be in more focus I would prefer<br/>Lighting: it''s a tad bit dark.  Esp in bottom left and behind the ear of the person.  <br/>Contrast: could use a tiny step up<br/>Communication: TV is communication so you meet the goal<br/>Intrigue: It''s really not that interesting to me, personally.  It gets the point across, but I don''t particularly feel drawn to it when looking at 50 pictures around it.  It doesn''t catch me and draw me in.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps you!<br/>Best to you!!!</td>', 'I saw your thread on "freaking hypocrits" post and i wanted to offer you my critique to maybe help you out a little.   Composition: it works well, but could be cropped a tiny bit tighter on the top and a little looser on the bottomColor: way too blue.  I would say you should warm this up a bit for a more natural lookFocus: the fingers are clear in some locations (i see one pretty clear finger nail) and a few buttons on the remote are clear, but not enough clarity in the image.  The DOF is fine for the face and body, but the hand and remote should be in more focus I would preferLighting: it''s a tad bit dark.  Esp in bottom left and behind the ear of the person.  Contrast: could use a tiny step upCommunication: TV is communication so you meet the goalIntrigue: It''s really not that interesting to me, personally.  It gets the point across, but I don''t particularly feel drawn to it when looking at 50 pictures around it.  It doesn''t catch me and draw me in. I hope this helps you!Best to you!!!', '2004-10-20 13:48:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(966896, 112508, 28201, '<td valign="top">I originally didn''t like this photo the first time I saw it, I just kind of passed it by and didn''t rate it.. Then about 10 minutes later I was just craving to see it again.  I figured any photo that got into my head like that was doing something right.  I still don''t know that I "like" it, but something about it makes me want to see it..  you got my 10..</td>', 'I originally didn''t like this photo the first time I saw it, I just kind of passed it by and didn''t rate it.. Then about 10 minutes later I was just craving to see it again.  I figured any photo that got into my head like that was doing something right.  I still don''t know that I "like" it, but something about it makes me want to see it..  you got my 10..', '2004-10-20 14:02:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(966924, 112230, 22824, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nruter:</b></div><hr/><i> This would be better if taken at night. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Maybe.  However, I don''t have a tripod, and due to the necessary longer exposure needed, hard to come out with shots that aren''t even a little blurry.<br/> <br/>But thanks for the tip.</td>', 'Originally posted by nruter: This would be better if taken at night.   Maybe.  However, I don''t have a tripod, and due to the necessary longer exposure needed, hard to come out with shots that aren''t even a little blurry. But thanks for the tip.', '2004-10-20 14:16:00.000000', NULL, 0),
