(973334, 111259, 24990, '<td valign="top">*CC*<br/>This is a good angled shot, the mist adds a nice effect, the softness of the image adds to the mist, and the sense of being lost.<br/>I would have liked the colours to be a bit stronger maybe....But seeing as this is a misty picture, then obviously they are going to seem watered down anyway..<br/>But a very nice photo, with a slight humour element which is nice.</td>', '*CC*This is a good angled shot, the mist adds a nice effect, the softness of the image adds to the mist, and the sense of being lost.I would have liked the colours to be a bit stronger maybe....But seeing as this is a misty picture, then obviously they are going to seem watered down anyway..But a very nice photo, with a slight humour element which is nice.', '2004-10-25 17:52:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(973345, 111650, 24990, '<td valign="top">*CC*<br/>Image is lovely, nice use of B&amp;W, the contrasts make this a powerful image, just a small problem with this pic (IMHO), and it is that the horizon seems to be coming from his ears...but a great shot nonetheless, I love the sky and reflections in the water...<br/></td>', '*CC*Image is lovely, nice use of B&W, the contrasts make this a powerful image, just a small problem with this pic (IMHO), and it is that the horizon seems to be coming from his ears...but a great shot nonetheless, I love the sky and reflections in the water...', '2004-10-25 17:59:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(973350, 112284, 24990, '<td valign="top">*CC*<br/>As some of the other commentors say, "Just a snapshot" or something similar.. but IMHO it is COMMUNICATION, it''s telling the world what is is, and even if you cant read, then there are still pictures... so good take on the subject in hand, maybe a slightly boring subject (hey it''s a sign) but taken at the angle it has been means it is still more interesting than a full on frontal shot.  Image is sharp and you can read it.. nicely exposed too.</td>', '*CC*As some of the other commentors say, "Just a snapshot" or something similar.. but IMHO it is COMMUNICATION, it''s telling the world what is is, and even if you cant read, then there are still pictures... so good take on the subject in hand, maybe a slightly boring subject (hey it''s a sign) but taken at the angle it has been means it is still more interesting than a full on frontal shot.  Image is sharp and you can read it.. nicely exposed too.', '2004-10-25 18:05:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(974115, 112297, 27034, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scalvert:</b></div><hr/><i> With this DOF, the focus is on the starlings rather than the communication equipment. It would help if one or more of the birds had its beak open. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your comments, both good ideas that I didn''t think of... maybe next time. Liz</td>', 'Originally posted by scalvert: With this DOF, the focus is on the starlings rather than the communication equipment. It would help if one or more of the birds had its beak open.   Thanks for your comments, both good ideas that I didn''t think of... maybe next time. Liz', '2004-10-26 09:03:11.000000', NULL, 0),
